# .env.example — copy to .env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# Nothing in CI reads this. The Godot gates, the spec validator and the agent-data
# check all run without an .env — only the two Atlassian scripts at the repo root
# need one, and only if you are generating or posting a status report.
#
# Both scripts parse ./.env themselves, line by line, with no python-dotenv:
# `KEY=value`, one per line, `#` comments and blank lines skipped. There is no
# quoting, no interpolation and no multi-line support — a value containing `=`
# is fine (only the first `=` splits), but a quoted value keeps its quotes.
#
# direnv also loads this file via `.envrc` (`dotenv`), so a `cd` into the repo
# exports these into the shell.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required — the two Atlassian scripts exit 1 without these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Your Atlassian site host. Host only: no scheme, no trailing slash, no /wiki.
# The scripts build "https://$ATLASSIAN_URL" themselves.
ATLASSIAN_URL=your-site.atlassian.net

# base64 of "email:api_token" — NOT the raw token. Mint the token at
# https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens then:
#
#     printf '%s' "you@example.com:your_api_token" | base64 -w0
#
# (drop -w0 on macOS/BSD base64). Both scripts also accept the older name
# ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN_BASE64_USEREMAIL; they check this one first. If you have
# only the legacy name set, they still work — see the comment in
# generate_report.py, which explains why both are honoured.
ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN_BASE64=

# Jira project key the report is built from — read by generate_report.py only.
# It was hardcoded to a deprecated board until 2026-07-28, which is why it is
# configuration now rather than a constant.
#
# Do not guess this value and do not copy it between projects: the keys, which
# board is deprecated, and which belong to the owner's other repositories are
# all recorded in docs/delivery-coordinates.md, the designated authority (D-026).
ATLASSIAN_JIRA_PROJECT_KEY=

# Confluence page the status report is posted under — read by
# post_to_confluence.py only. The space is resolved from this page, so there is
# no separate space variable to set.
#
# It was a constant in the script until 2026-07-31, for the same reason the Jira
# key was: nobody had needed to point it anywhere else. Same rule as above — do
# not guess it, and do not copy it between projects. docs/delivery-coordinates.md
# is the authority (D-026).
#
# There is no fallback. An unreachable page exits 1 rather than posting
# somewhere else, because a silent fallback is how reports once landed in a
# sibling product's space.
ATLASSIAN_CONFLUENCE_PARENT_PAGE_ID=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional — used to derive the credential above, read by nothing here
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keeping the two halves around makes the base64 reproducible without minting a
# new token. No script in this repo reads either.
#ATLASSIAN_EMAIL=you@example.com
#ATLASSIAN_API_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bridge authentication — read by bridge/ modules
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key for the bridge (Messages API + Agent SDK).
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not read by anything in this repository
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These turn up in real .env files here because direnv exports them to the whole
# shell and outside tooling picks them up — model CLIs, gstack, review helpers.
# They are listed so their absence is not mistaken for a missing requirement,
# and so nobody adds a repo script that quietly depends on one. If a script here
# ever does need one, document it in the required section above instead.
#
#   CONFLUENCE_SPACE_KEY / CONFLUENCE_SPACE_URL
#       post_to_confluence.py does NOT read these. It resolves the space from
#       ATLASSIAN_CONFLUENCE_PARENT_PAGE_ID above, so the space needs no
#       variable of its own.
#   OPENAI_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT, NODE_ENV
#       external tooling only. There is no JavaScript in this repo, so NODE_ENV
#       affects nothing here; see CLAUDE.md § Commands on what package.json is.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Verify
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A correct .env makes this print a summary and write report.md. A wrong one
# names the missing variables and exits 1 — it does not raise KeyError:
#
#     python3 generate_report.py
#
# Never commit .env, and never paste a token into an issue, PR or commit
# message. If one is exposed, rotating it at the link above is the only fix —
# deleting the commit or closing the ticket does not revoke it.
